WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.130
EDGAR estimates that Germany's emissions
fell from 1,227 to 660 million tonnes

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.110
of CO₂ equivalent between 1990 and 2025.

3
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.310
Complainants, some of them very young
and some living in Bangladesh and Nepal,

4
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.590
challenged Germany's Federal
Climate Change Act of December 2019.

5
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.510
On 24 March 2021, the Federal Constitutional
Court found the complaints partially

6
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.350
successful, but not for the
complainants in Bangladesh and Nepal.

7
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.290
So who really changes climate action?

8
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.630
Only governments?

9
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.130
Only voters, every few years?

10
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.750
In this mission, you'll
map the stakeholders,

11
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.150
from citizens to energy
companies and investors.

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.570
Then you'll weigh why
their perspectives differ,

13
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.310
by need, practicality and urgency.

14
00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:57.390
Your mission: explain how people outside
government can change climate action.
